{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Now the man Moses was exceedingly humble.</b> The verse informs us of this here, for according to what we have written — that they spoke in his presence — the verse gives the reason why HaShem needed to do all that is stated in the matter: because the man Moses was exceedingly humble, and on account of his humility he refrained from giving them the answer that the situation required, so that they would know the difference between the prophecy of Moses and that of the other prophets. And it was precise to say <b>more than any man who is upon the face of the earth</b>, to establish definitively that the withholding of an answer from him in this matter was due to this: for a man whose self-perception is beneath, Heaven forbid, all who are upon the face of the earth — how could it be conceived, Heaven forbid, that he would give an answer implying that he is greater than all the prophets? Therefore the utterance from HaShem came and He answered them <b>suddenly</b> — because they were mistreating (לשון אונאה) Moses with words, and it is written (Amos 7:7–8): ״הִנֵּה יְהֹוָה נִצָּב עַל חוֹמַת אֲנָךְ״, and our Sages, of blessed memory, said (Yalkut): suddenly — close to scattering, etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The word פִּתְאוֹם ('suddenly') and the Yalkut citation are rendered as they stand; the ellipsis 'וכו׳' (etc.) is preserved from the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:08.654236133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}